  "id": "BIT-postgresql-2026-120144",
  "summary": "PostgreSQL type-cache invalidation gap executes arbitrary code",
  "details": "Type confusion from incomplete PostgreSQL type-cache invalidation allows an object creator to execute arbitrary code as the operating system user running the database, via a composite type change while its cache entry is being populated.  Within major version 18, minor versions before PostgreSQL 18.7 are affected.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18 are unaffected.",
